  "finalText": "The **Pulse 2** title sequence is built in the Main comp (1920×1080, 30 fps, 10 s). It scores 89/100 in the critic.\n\n- **Feature words (0–3 s):** **Word 1 - 40h battery**, **Word 2 - Spatial audio** (orange) and **Word 3 - Pure silence** land on the bar downbeats at 0, 1 and 2 s. Each uses a different snap: a scale punch, a whip from the right, and a rotation snap. They cut hard on the next beat.\n- **Name slam (3–6 s):** An orange full-frame **Orange flash** hits at 3 s. **PULSE 2** slams from 170% to 100% with Expo Out, and the **Shockwave ring** expands from the wordmark and fades.\n- **Available now (6–10 s):** **PULSE 2** rises to make room, and the orange **Available now pill** (plus its text) springs in at 6.3 s. It then breathes gently until the end.\n\nPalette is #0B0B0D background, #FF5A1F orange and #F5F5F5 type, all in Inter 900.\n\nChoices to know about:\n- There's no audio file, so the 120 BPM is imagined. Hits are placed on beat multiples (0, 1, 2, 3, 6 s), and I added five markers at those points rather than one per beat.\n- The word whips and the punchy scale-in on \"40h battery\" are deliberately snappier than the handbook's timing tables, so the critic's notes on those are intentional.\n\nNext I could sync the hits to a real track, tighten the shockwave stroke (it thickens as it scales), or add a subtle push-in over the hold."
